nician is  following the latest calibration method  associated instruments testing the  quality of results  this is about the traceability so this  is absolutely essential for 17.025  compliance in a third-party testing lab  but it is useful in an in-house testing  lab  what it means is that if there is  liability  if there is a question well how do we  know  that the instrument that the test result  that you gave was done on an  instrument that was properly maintained  and calibrated  not today but at the time the test was  done  so you need an association between the  calibration  date and the date on which the test was  done  the limbs will track all of that the  limbs will say here you can see with our  traceability  that the particular test was done on  such and such date  here was the previous calibration here  was the sop that was followed for that  calibration  so you have a completely traceable  record showing that your instrument was  calibrated and maintained  manage documents with limbs this is all  of your sops  so the second thing that would come up  in that same liability question  is when the test was done was the  correct sop followed  this will show it to you only the latest  sop was available  and the sop that was used for any  particular test distract  this is useful in the case of a recall  of a test method  the instrument manufacturers this  doesn't happen often but they can say  there was something wrong with the sop  we issued  and the test results need to be  invalidated instead of needing to  invalidate  all of your tests with the limbs it'll  tell you  only these tests were done using this  sop  so these are the only tests we need to  redo  manage staff and training you have a  whole bunch of staff and they all need  to be trained  for each step of your extraction process  and  each step of your testing process so  here you can see two different training  courses  ion exchange chromatography and paper  chromatography  and in the ion exchan